WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:04.920
It looks like "Creed III is going the distance.&nbsp;
It's a franchise movie with big-name stars,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:08.160
but its box office take is still&nbsp;
shattering expectations. How is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:10.260
this boxing epic punching&nbsp;
so high above its weight?

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:15.000
The first two "Creed" movies were released on&nbsp;
Wednesdays over the Thanksgiving holiday weekend.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:19.800
"Creed III," by contrast, opened on a Friday&nbsp;
over a weekend with no major holidays. Since&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:23.640
it wasn't burning off demand with a Wednesday&nbsp;
launch, it's no shock "Creed III" had a bigger&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:27.420
three-day opening weekend than its predecessors.&nbsp;
What's impressive, though, is that "Creed III"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:31.620
left the five-day hauls of the first two "Creed"&nbsp;
films in the dust over just three days with its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:37.320
staggering $58.4 million take. "Creed II made&nbsp;
$56 million over its first five days of release.

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:39.060
"I'm comin' for everything!"

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:43.860
"Creed III" was even further ahead of the first&nbsp;
"Creed," which made $42 million in its first five&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:48.360
days. It took 11 days for the first "Creed" to&nbsp;
narrowly exceed what "Creed III" amassed in three.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:52.860
Comparing the opening weekend of "Creed III" to&nbsp;
the original "Rocky" movies is a bit trickier&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:57.240
since those movies were released in a drastically&nbsp;
different time, but it's worth noting "Creed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.240 --> 00:01:02.880
III" did nearly five times the $12.1 million&nbsp;
debut of the 2006 installment "Rocky Balboa."

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:08.340
"Creed III" was one of the first films released&nbsp;
by MGM since Amazon scooped up the legendary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:13.020
studio. MGM and sister company, Orion Pictures,&nbsp;
have released a handful of smaller titles into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:17.040
theaters since the acquisition, including "Women&nbsp;
Talking" and "Bones and All," but "Creed III"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:21.420
is the first massive MGM release under Amazon&nbsp;
ownership. So the movie's opening weekend made&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:25.380
history for Amazon by outgrossing the domestic&nbsp;
hauls of every other flick in Amazon history.

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:30.360
That includes not just recent MGM and Orion&nbsp;
releases, but all other Amazon Studios films,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:34.860
including "Manchester by the Sea" and "The Big&nbsp;
Sick." To be fair, many of Amazon's previous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:38.640
theatrical releases were arthouse fare that&nbsp;
never played in more than a couple hundred&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:42.420
theaters. "You Were Never Really Here," for&nbsp;
instance, was never expected to be a moneymaker&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:46.260
like a "Creed" movie could be. So the success&nbsp;
of this sequel opens more doors for Amazon.

00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:51.000
The massive debut of "Creed III" demonstrates&nbsp;
that Amazon is capable of launching MGM movies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:55.200
in a big way, and redefines the level of box&nbsp;
office success the company's movies can reach.

00:01:55.920 --> 00:02:00.000
Sports dramas usually need a little time&nbsp;
to warm up at the box office. For example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:03.060
you may remember a little movie&nbsp;
called "Remember the Titans." That&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:06.780
inspirational classic opened with under&nbsp;
$25 million at the weekend box office,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:10.200
and still pulled in a sizable domestic&nbsp;
haul thanks to positive word-of-mouth.

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:14.400
Most sports dramas aren't big franchise fare,&nbsp;
so they're less likely to open like movies that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:18.660
are. This meant that "Creed III," the newest&nbsp;
movie in a long-running, storied series, had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:22.920
no trouble scoring the biggest domestic opening&nbsp;
weekend in history for a sports drama. It took&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:28.080
the crown away from the $35.5 million debut of&nbsp;
none other than its own predecessor, "Creed II."

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:31.560
No matter how you slice it, it's pretty&nbsp;
impressive just how far ahead of all other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:35.940
sports movies the third "Creed" entry ran in&nbsp;
its first three days of release. Previously,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:39.240
no sports drama ever had cracked&nbsp;
$40 million in an opening weekend,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:43.380
and "Creed III" shattered that mark. "Creed&nbsp;
III" even exceeded the entire lifetime&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.380 --> 00:02:48.260
domestic hauls of well-regarded sports dramas like&nbsp;
"Invincible" and "Southpaw" in just one weekend.

00:02:48.260 --> 00:02:51.660
"A man can only take so much failure."

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:56.640
Michael B. Jordan has been selective about where&nbsp;
he shows up, with the actor only headlining two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.640 --> 00:03:00.960
other theatrical releases, "Just Mercy" and "A&nbsp;
Journal for Jordan," since the release of "Creed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:05.220
II." He's made cameos in other movies with varying&nbsp;
degrees of success, including Black Panther:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:09.780
Wakanda Forever" on the positive side, and&nbsp;
"Space Jam: A New Legacy" on the… other side.

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:13.500
"I was just gettin' some popcorn,&nbsp;
and then this cat grabbed me."

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:17.580
Except for that one exception – as well&nbsp;
as streaming movies like the Tom Clancy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:20.940
thriller "Without Remorse" – he's generally&nbsp;
shown a good deal of shrewdness when it comes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:25.080
to selecting his projects, which has helped keep&nbsp;
him from being too overexposed as a leading man.

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:29.760
With that in mind, Jordan doesn't have a sprawling&nbsp;
box office track record to his name. With the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:33.840
major exception of the first "Black Panther," he's&nbsp;
never appeared in a movie that cracked $40 million&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.840 --> 00:03:38.760
on its three-day opening weekend — until "Creed&nbsp;
III." In just three days, "Creed III" exceeded&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:43.140
the lifetime grosses of many other theatrical&nbsp;
releases Jordan appeared in, such as the 2015&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:48.000
"Fantastic Four" reboot and "Red Tails." While&nbsp;
it's clear audiences like Jordan as a presence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:52.500
"Creed III" blew away all expectations for how&nbsp;
big a Michael B. Jordan star vehicle could go.

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:56.400
In general, "Rocky" movies have&nbsp;
been holiday season staples.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:59.280
While the second and third "Rocky"&nbsp;
entries each opened in the summer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:02.640
the other original "Rocky" movies all&nbsp;
hit theaters in November and December.

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:06.720
It's a timeframe that's served the franchise&nbsp;
well, especially since the all-ages appeal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:10.200
and uplifting spirit of the franchise feels&nbsp;
like the perfect thing families can watch&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:14.040
together during the holidays. The first two&nbsp;
"Creed" movies also opened over Thanksgiving,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:17.580
but "Creed III" went in a different&nbsp;
direction with its March 2023 release.

00:04:17.580 --> 00:04:21.540
It's reasonable to assume that there was some&nbsp;
trepidation about an early-spring release,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.540 --> 00:04:25.320
but even if there was, there turned out&nbsp;
to be nothing to worry about. March has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:29.400
actually become a go-to month for blockbuster&nbsp;
hits, with "The Batman" finding success in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:34.440
2022 and "Captain Marvel" doing the same&nbsp;
in 2019, among many others. Release date&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:37.920
traditions served the "Rocky" movies well&nbsp;
in the past, but "Creed III" excelling in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:41.640
March proved that it's okay to do something a&nbsp;
little unexpected to throw off your opponents.

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:46.860
Third movies in franchises are tricky. Unlike&nbsp;
a second installment, audiences need a little&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:50.340
something more than just "this character is&nbsp;
back" to get them into the theater. That's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.340 --> 00:04:54.060
why many third installments make noticeably&nbsp;
less than the second entry in a franchise.

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:57.060
"Harry Potter and the Prisoner of Azkaban,"&nbsp;
[AZZ-kuh-ban] for instance, had the lowest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.060 --> 00:05:01.980
domestic gross for any "Harry Potter" film until&nbsp;
the "Fantastic Beasts" movies came along. And "The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.980 --> 00:05:06.180
Hangover: Part III" made substantially less in&nbsp;
North America than either of its predecessors.

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:09.900
There was reason to assume "Creed III"&nbsp;
could suffer the same box office fate as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:13.680
so many other third installments, especially&nbsp;
if you consider it as the ninth movie in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:17.340
larger "Rocky" franchise. Yet the film's&nbsp;
opening weekend showed a franchise with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.340 --> 00:05:21.060
lots of gas left in the tank. Barring&nbsp;
catastrophic weekend-to-weekend dips,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:24.840
"Creed III" will have no problem surpassing&nbsp;
the lifetime North American hauls of the first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:29.880
two "Creed" movies, an impressive feat and one&nbsp;
that's incredibly rare among third installments.

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:36.420
Since "Black Panther: Wakanda Forever's" massive&nbsp;
$181.3 million opening weekend in November 2022,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.420 --> 00:05:40.560
only two other movies have managed to crack&nbsp;
$40 million in their domestic opening weekends:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:44.580
"Avatar: The Way of Water" and "Ant-Man&nbsp;
and the Wasp: Quantumania." Of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.580 --> 00:05:47.880
"M3GAN" and "Cocaine Bear" proved to&nbsp;
be surprise sleeper hits, but there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:51.180
haven't been a ton of tentpole releases&nbsp;
to drum up significant opening weekends.

00:05:51.180 --> 00:05:55.680
That means "Creed III," scored the third-biggest&nbsp;
domestic opening weekend since "Wakanda Forever,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.680 --> 00:05:59.640
and the second-biggest single-weekend&nbsp;
haul in 2023 to date. Impressively,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.640 --> 00:06:03.180
"Creed III" managed the 18th-biggest&nbsp;
domestic opening weekend for any movie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.180 --> 00:06:06.600
since the COVID-19 pandemic shut&nbsp;
down movie theaters in March 2020,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.600 --> 00:06:11.160
with many of the titles that surpassed it carrying&nbsp;
significantly bigger budgets and marketing spends.

00:06:11.820 --> 00:06:16.020
With the original "Rocky" movies, sequels&nbsp;
came out at a rapid pace. Across the first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:19.380
four installments, audiences never had to&nbsp;
wait more than three years to see where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.380 --> 00:06:23.760
Rocky Balboa was going next. This steady pace&nbsp;
ended up backfiring on the franchise, though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.760 --> 00:06:28.680
when "Rocky V" took so long to make. A five-year&nbsp;
wait ended up killing the financial momentum of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.680 --> 00:06:32.460
this saga, with "Rocky V" making drastically&nbsp;
less than its predecessors in North America.

00:06:32.460 --> 00:06:37.740
"Rocky Balboa" and "Creed" did fine at the box&nbsp;
office despite coming off lengthy hiatuses. If&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.740 --> 00:06:41.760
anything the long waits helped those flicks&nbsp;
because they were legacy sequels. A lengthy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:44.880
wait time gave them their emotional&nbsp;
oomph. Traditional "Rocky" sequels,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:47.280
judging by the original films,&nbsp;
needed to be made quickly.

00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:51.180
So one might have guessed that "Creed III"&nbsp;
arriving nearly five years after "Creed II"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.180 --> 00:06:55.620
could've tanked the "Creed" movies financially.&nbsp;
Instead, "Creed III" once again bucked the trend.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.620 --> 00:07:00.180
If anything, the wait seems to have made the&nbsp;
hearts of moviegoers grow fonder for Adonis Creed.

00:07:00.780 --> 00:07:03.720
"Creed III" was never expected to&nbsp;
be a lightweight at the box office,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.720 --> 00:07:07.380
but initial tracking for its opening weekend&nbsp;
didn't suggest it would shatter box office&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.380 --> 00:07:12.540
records. Pro Box Office reported at the start of&nbsp;
February 2023 that "Creed III" was tracking for a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.540 --> 00:07:18.000
$25 million to $34 million domestic debut. On the&nbsp;
low end, that meant "Creed III" would've opened&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:22.380
considerably beneath its predecessors, though&nbsp;
a $34 million take would've at least been ahead&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.380 --> 00:07:26.640
of the first "Creed." As late as one week before&nbsp;
its release, Pro Box Office was still predicting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.640 --> 00:07:31.200
"Creed III" would open as low as $29 million in&nbsp;
its first three days of release in North America.

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:35.760
Many industry insiders assumed that there&nbsp;
was nowhere to go but down after "Creed II."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:41.040
Just days before its debut, Deadline predicted&nbsp;
"Creed III" would take in $38 to $40 million,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:44.700
bigger than earlier tracking projections&nbsp;
but still nowhere near what "Creed III"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.700 --> 00:07:48.540
would end up amassing on opening weekend.&nbsp;
The sum "Creed III" ended up amassing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.540 --> 00:07:51.600
was more than double the lowest initial&nbsp;
tracking figures for its opening weekend.

00:07:52.800 --> 00:07:56.880
The ending of "Creed II" gave Sylvester&nbsp;
Stallone an out to leave the franchise behind.

00:07:58.020 --> 00:07:59.220
"It's your time."

00:08:03.840 --> 00:08:08.220
The film's final moments saw Rocky Balboa&nbsp;
finally traveling to Chicago to visit his son,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.220 --> 00:08:12.600
Rocky Balboa Jr., and grandson, Logan.&nbsp;
It was a reunion that suggested that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:16.860
despite all the turmoil of the past, Balboa&nbsp;
could have a happy future with his loved ones.

00:08:16.860 --> 00:08:20.640
Stallone made clear that he wouldn't be&nbsp;
returning to the role of Rocky in "Creed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.640 --> 00:08:24.000
III" in an interview with The Hollywood&nbsp;
Reporter, saying the tone of the movie was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:28.020
darker than what he would have preferred.&nbsp;
Variety also noted that Stallone has bad&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.020 --> 00:08:31.560
blood with series producer Irwin Winkler&nbsp;
over ownership of the Rocky character,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.560 --> 00:08:34.740
a sign he might never return to the&nbsp;
role that kick started his career.

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:39.300
So there was some question as to how successful&nbsp;
"Creed III" would be without Rocky on the poster,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.300 --> 00:08:43.860
but clearly, it wasn't a problem. Impressively,&nbsp;
the film's North America opening weekend even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.860 --> 00:08:48.360
managed to surpass the opening three-day grosses&nbsp;
of every single movie Sylvester Stallone has ever&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:52.440
appeared in with the exception of "Guardians&nbsp;
of the Galaxy Vol. 2." At the end of the day,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.440 --> 00:08:56.280
"Creed III" didn't just manage to survive&nbsp;
without Stallone; it's surpassing the box&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.280 --> 00:08:59.340
office track record of the man who was&nbsp;
long the focal point of the franchise.

00:09:00.180 --> 00:09:05.220
"Creed III" was the first of an intense slate&nbsp;
of movies in March 2023. New installments in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.220 --> 00:09:08.940
"Scream," "Shazam!," and "John Wick" franchises&nbsp;
are all opening while "Dungeons and Dragons:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:13.020
Honor Among Thieves" is also prepped to debut at&nbsp;
the end of the month. With so many high-profile&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.020 --> 00:09:16.800
motion pictures poised to fight for dollars and&nbsp;
the attention of moviegoers in a single month,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.800 --> 00:09:20.040
it's easy to see a scenario where "Creed&nbsp;
III" could have gotten lost in the shuffle.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:24.480
Perhaps there just wouldn't be room for a boxing&nbsp;
drama amidst all the superheroes and assassins.

00:09:24.480 --> 00:09:28.380
Instead, "Creed III" opened up with a&nbsp;
bang and set a high bar. If anything,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:31.800
the success of "Creed III" puts added&nbsp;
pressure on the fourth "John Wick" to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:34.860
surpass the box office haul of its&nbsp;
predecessors. "Creed III" kicked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.860 --> 00:09:37.740
off one of the most loaded months in&nbsp;
recent memory with impressive style.

00:09:37.740 --> 00:09:42.900
Much of the buzz around "Ant-Man and the Wasp:&nbsp;
Quantumania" since its release has surrounded&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:42.900 --> 00:09:46.920
its sharp box office decline, with the feature&nbsp;
experiencing the worst second-weekend drop ever&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.920 --> 00:09:50.940
for a Marvel Cinematic Universe movie. The&nbsp;
trend continued with the film's third-weekend&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.940 --> 00:09:56.040
decline of 60%, which indicates that the&nbsp;
second-weekend drop was no fluke. "Quantumania"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.040 --> 00:10:00.120
is being weighed down by dismal audience&nbsp;
word-of-mouth after a solid opening weekend.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.120 --> 00:10:04.200
This lack of staying power is especially&nbsp;
interesting to see in comparison to "Creed III,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:08.460
which showed remarkable stamina on a day-to-day&nbsp;
basis during its first few days of release.

00:10:08.460 --> 00:10:14.160
At Thursday night showings, "Creed III" secured&nbsp;
$5.5 million from moviegoers, a sizeable take&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:14.160 --> 00:10:19.620
that already put it on track for a great opening&nbsp;
weekend. Its subsequent $58.4 million debut was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:19.620 --> 00:10:23.820
more than 10 times its Thursday night haul,&nbsp;
an impressive amount of retention, indicating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.820 --> 00:10:27.900
that "Creed III" was attracting audiences all&nbsp;
throughout the weekend. For comparison's sake,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.900 --> 00:10:33.840
"Bullet Train" did $4.6 million at Thursday night&nbsp;
showings and ended up doing $30.1 million for its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:33.840 --> 00:10:38.520
first weekend, or about 6-and-a-half times its&nbsp;
Thursday night haul. The lack of frontloading in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.520 --> 00:10:42.840
the opening weekend of "Creed III" underscores how&nbsp;
impressive its debut was, especially since it was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.840 --> 00:10:46.440
coming hot off the wheels of "Quantumania,"&nbsp;
which had very poor box office retention.

